---
import PortraitRotator from "../components/PortraitRotator";
import { buttonClasses } from "../components/ui/Button";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pt-10 pb-12">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.4fr_1fr]">
      <h1
        class="max-w-3xl text-balance font-sans text-6xl sm:text-7xl font-semibold leading-[1.2] text-ink"
      >
        In a crowd of <br class="hidden lg:inline" />
        <span class="font-serif font-semibold italic text-accent-ink">67 million</span>,{" "}<br class="hidden lg:inline" />
        how many look{" "}<br class="hidden lg:inline" />
        just like you?
      </h1>

      <div class="flex flex-col justify-end gap-6 pb-2">
        <p class="max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">
          “Anonymised” datasets are rarely anonymous. With few everyday details such as approximate location or demographics, our model trained on census data can
          pick a single person out of an entire country.
        </p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <a href="/quiz" class={buttonClasses({ size: "lg" })}>Take the quiz →</a>
          <span class="text-sm text-ink">&lt;2 minutes</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-navy/50">
      <PortraitRotator client:visible />
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-sm text-ink">
      Built by privacy researchers at Oxford, Imperial College London and UCLouvain, using data across 103 countries
      from IPUMS, the world's largest collection of national census. The underlying mathematical model was published in{" "}
      <a class="underline" href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-019-10933-3">Nature Communications</a>.
      Everything runs in your browser.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
